        solution: {
            text: String.raw`Lattice energy is described by Coulomb’s law, increasing with the product of ionic charges and decreasing with

ionic radii. \ce{NaCl} and \ce{KBr} both have ions with a charge of 1+ and 1−, while \ce{MgO} and \ce{SrS} have ions with charges of 2+ and 2−. \ce{MgO} will have a smaller ionic radius than \ce{SrS} due to the less electron layers of \ce{Mg} and O. Thus, the

correct answer is \ce{MgO}, or $B$.`,
            image: ["/assets/local/2010_local_54_solution.png"]
        }
