        id: "2013_local_58",
        exam_type: "local",
        year: 2013,
        number: 58,
        topic: "Organic/Biochemistry",
        question: String.raw`Which statement does not describe benzene, \ce{C6H6}?`,
        question_image: false,
        answer: "B",
        answer_image: false,
        choices: {
            A: "It is an aromatic hydrocarbon.",
            B: "It exists in two isomeric forms.",
            C: "It undergoes substitution reactions.",
            D: String.raw`It can react to form three different products with the formula \ce{C6H4Cl2}.`
        },
        images: {
            image: ["/assets/local/2013_local_58.png"],
            question_image: ["/assets/local/2013_local_58_question.png"],
            subtext: null
        },
        solution: {
            text: String.raw`Let us analyze the answer choices.

\begin{itemize}
  \item A: Benzene \ce{(C6H6)} is one of the most famous aromatic hydrocarbons.
  \item B: It does not exist in two isomeric forms. Two possible structures can be drawn, but these are resonance structures.
  \item C: It is reticent towards addition reactions, but it is capable of undergoing substitution reactions.
  \item D: There are three different ways (ortho, meta, and para) to place two chlorine substituents around the ring, in \ce{C6H4Cl2} by replacing hydrogen with chlorine.
\end{itemize}

However, benzene does not exist in two isomeric forms. Thus, only $B$ is false.`,
            image: ["/assets/local/2013_local_58_solution.png"]
        }
