        id: "2014_local_36",
        exam_type: "local",
        year: 2014,
        number: 36,
        topic: "Equilibrium",
        question: String.raw`What will be the result when 15.0~mL of 0.040~M lead(II) nitrate is mixed with 15.0~mL of 0.040~M sodium chloride?
\[ \ce{PbCl2(s)}\ce{Pb^2+(aq)} + \text{2 }\ce{Cl-(aq)}\text{ [}\mathrm{K}_{\mathrm{sp}} = 1.7 \times 10^{-5}\text{]} \]`,
        question_image: false,
        answer: "A",
        answer_image: false,
        choices: {
            A: "A clear solution with no precipitate will result.",
            B: String.raw`Solid \ce{PbCl2} will precipitate and excess \ce{Pb^2+} ions will remain in solution.`,
            C: String.raw`Solid \ce{PbCl2} will precipitate and excess \ce{Cl-} ions will remain in solution.`,
            D: String.raw`Solid \ce{PbCl2} will precipitate and no excess ions will remain in solution.`
        },
        images: {
            image: ["/assets/local/2014_local_36.png"],
            question_image: ["/assets/local/2014_local_36_question.png"],
            subtext: null
        },
        solution: {
            text: String.raw`Calculate $Q$, the reaction quotient, and then compare it to the $K_{\mathrm{sp}}$.
\[ \ce{[Pb^2+]} = \text{0⋅040 M }\times\text{ 15⋅0 mL15.0 mL} + \text{15.0 mL} = \text{0⋅020 M} \]
\[ \ce{[Cl-]} = \text{0⋅040 M }\times\text{ 15⋅0 mL15.0 mL} + \text{15.0 mL} = \text{0⋅020 M} \]
\[ \text{Calculating }Q\text{, we get} \]
\[ Q = \ce{[Pb^2+][Cl-]2} \]
\[ Q = (0.020)(0.020)^{2} = 8.0 \times 10^{-6} \]
If $Q < K_{\mathrm{sp}}$, then the solution will be unsaturated and there will be no precipitate. However, if $Q > K_{\mathrm{sp}}$, then the

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{lcc}
\hline
reaction will shift left until $Q = K$, forming precipitate. Comparing, we see $Q < K_{\mathrm{sp}}$, so & \textbf{no precipitate} & \textbf{will form.} \\
\hline
This leads us to $A$. &  &  \\
$8.0 \times 10^{-6} < 1.7 \times 10^{-5}$ &  &  \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}`,
            image: ["/assets/local/2014_local_36_solution.png"]
        }
