        exam_type: "local",
        year: 2017,
        number: 10,
        topic: "Descriptive/Laboratory",
        question: String.raw`Addition of small amounts of which solids to 4~M \ce{HCl} will result in gas evolution?

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \ce{Zn}
  \item \ce{Na2SO3}
\end{enumerate}`,
        question_image: false,
        answer: "C",
        answer_image: false,
        choices: {
            A: "I only",
            B: "II only",
            C: "Both I and II",
            D: "Neither I nor II"
        },
        images: {
            image: ["/assets/local/2017_local_10.png"],
            question_image: ["/assets/local/2017_local_10_question.png"],
            subtext: null
        },
        solution: {
            text: String.raw`Reactive metals tend to react with acids by forming hydrogen gas. In this case, the

reaction is
\[ \ce{Zn(s) + 2 H+(aq) -> Zn^2+(aq) + H2(g)} \]
Thus $I$ is correct, as a gas evolution reaction. Looking at II, we see the reaction is
\[ \ce{SO3^2-(s) + 2 H+(aq) -> SO2(g) + H2O(l)} \]
\ce{SO2} is a gas, so this is also a gas evolution reaction. Thus the answer is $I$ + II, which is $C$.`,
            image: ["/assets/local/2017_local_10_solution.png"]
        }
