        year: 2020,
        number: 24,
        topic: "Thermodynamics",
        question: String.raw`A sample of water in a movable piston is maintained at $100.0\,^\circ\mathrm{C}$ with an external pressure $p$. Which statement best describes the transformation of some of the liquid water into water vapor?`,
        question_image: false,
        answer: "D",
        answer_image: false,
        choices: {
            A: String.raw`It is spontaneous if $p \geq 1$ atm.`,
            B: "It is reversible if $p = 1$ atm and spontaneous if $p > 1$ atm.",
            C: String.raw`It is nonspontaneous if $p \geq 1$ atm.`,
            D: "It is reversible if $p = 1$ atm and nonspontaneous if $p > 1$ atm."
        },
        images: {
            image: ["/assets/local/2020_local_24.png"],
            question_image: ["/assets/local/2020_local_24_question.png"],
            subtext: null
        },
        solution: {
            text: String.raw`At 1~atm and $100.0 ^{◦}\mathrm{C}$, water reaches its boiling point. This means that it can turn into

vapor if heat is added, or it can turn into liquid by releasing heat. Thus, the vaporization is reversible at 1~atm and $100.0 ^{◦}\mathrm{C}$. Now let’s think about the phase diagram of water. If we increase the pressure past 1~atm, water becomes a liquid, and the vaporization is no longer

spontaneous. Thus, the answer is $D$.`,
            image: ["/assets/local/2020_local_24_solution.png"]
        }
