        number: 5,
        topic: "Stoichiometry/Solutions",
        question: String.raw`1.00~g of hydrated potassium carbonate, $\mathrm{K}_{2}\mathrm{CO}_{3}\cdotn\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$, is heated to $250\,^\circ\mathrm{C}$ to give 0.836~g anhydrous \ce{K2CO3}. What is the value of $n$?`,
        question_image: false,
