        year: 2003,
        number: 12,
        topic: "Descriptive/Laboratory",
        question: String.raw`Benzene melts at $5.50\,^\circ\mathrm{C}$ and has a freezing point depression constant of $5.10\,^\circ\mathrm{C}\cdot\mathrm{m}^{-1}$. Calculate the freezing point of a solution that contains 0.0500 mole of acetic acid, \ce{CH3COOH}, in 125~g of benzene if acetic acid forms a dimer in this solvent.`,
