        year: 2003,
        number: 20,
        topic: "Thermodynamics",
        question: String.raw`When 50. mL of 0.10~M \ce{HCl} is mixed with 50. mL of 0.10~M \ce{NaOH} the temperature of the solution increases by $3.0\,^\circ\mathrm{C}$. Calculate the $\Delta H_{\mathrm{neutralization}}$ per mole of \ce{HCl}. (The solution has a density = $1.0 \mathrm{g}\cdot\mathrm{mL}^{-1}$ and $\mathrm{C}_{\mathrm{p}} = 4.2 \mathrm{J}\cdot\mathrm{g}^{-1}\cdot^\circ\mathrm{C}^{-1}$)`,
