        number: 54,
        topic: "Bonding/Molecular Structure",
        question: String.raw`Sulfur tetrafluoride adopts a see-saw geometry with two axial F atoms with a \ce{F-S-F} angle of about $180\,^\circ$ and two equatorial F atoms at about $90\,^\circ$ from the axial fluorines. Which statement most accurately describes the axial and equatorial \ce{S-F} bonds?`,
        question_image: false,
