        exam_type: "national-I",
        year: 2020,
        number: 33,
        topic: "Equilibrium",
        question: String.raw`The formation constant $K_{\mathrm{f}}$ of the hexamminecadmium ion, \ce{Cd(NH3)6^2+}, is $2.6 \times 10^{5}$. In a solution whose ammonia concentration is 0.12~M, what percentage of the cadmium in solution is in the form of \ce{Cd(NH3)6^2+}?`,
        question_image: false,
        answer: "A",
        answer_image: false,
