        exam_type: "national-I",
        year: 2021,
        number: 2,
        topic: "Stoichiometry/Solutions",
        question: String.raw`Potassium hydrogen phthalate (\ce{KHP}, $M = 204$) is a monoprotic acid used as a primary standard in acid-base titrations. It takes 28.15~mL of a solution of \ce{Sr(OH)2} to neutralize 0.402~g \ce{KHP}. What is the concentration of the \ce{Sr(OH)2} solution?`,
