        number: 6,
        topic: "Stoichiometry/Solutions",
        question: String.raw`A solution of 5.00~g oxalic acid (\ce{H2C2O4}, $M = 90.04$) in 100.0~g \ce{H2O} has a freezing point of $-1.31\,^\circ\mathrm{C}$. What is the percent ionization of oxalic acid in this solution? The freezing point depression constant of water is $K_{\mathrm{f}} = 1.86\,^\circ\mathrm{C} m^{-1}$.`,
        question_image: false,
        answer: "B",
        answer_image: false,
        choices: {
            A: String.raw`13.5\%`,
            B: String.raw`26.8\%`,
            C: String.raw`70.4\%`,
            D: String.raw`100\%`
        },
        images: {
            image: ["/assets/national-I/2021_national-I_6.png"],
            question_image: ["/assets/national-I/2021_national-I_6_question.png"],
            subtext: null
        },
        solution: {
            text: String.raw`Difficulty: Hard Learning Objectives: colligative properties; freezing point depression; van’t Hoff factor; percent ionization of acids

Please be aware that molality is used for colligative properties rather than molarity as molality is temperature independent. Molality is defined as the moles of solute divided by the mass of solvent in kg.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{lcc}
\hline
\textbf{is} & \textbf{According to the freezing point depression equation, the molality of all solute particles in the solution} &  \\
\hline
molality(particles) = $\Delta T^{\mathrm{f}}$ &  & 1.31 ℃ \\
$\mathrm{K}_{\mathrm{f}}$ & = & 1.86 ℃ $\mathrm{m}^{-1} = 0.704$ m \\
but not the identity of particles. We can conclude that oxalic acid is partially dissociated as follows: & The molality of the oxalic acid is 5.00~g/(90.04 $\mathrm{g}/\mathrm{mol}\times0.1000$ kg) = $0.555 m < 0.704 m$. As freezing point depression is a colligative property, which only depends on the number of the solute particles, &  \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
\[ \mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{A} \rightleftharpoons\ce{H+} + \mathrm{HA}^{-} \]
0.555 0 0

–x +x +x
\[ \text{0.555–x }x\text{ x} \]
\[ \text{Total molality} = 0.555 - x + x + x = 0.704\text{, }x = 0.149 \]
So, the percent ionization of the acid is 0.149/0.555 = 26.8\%, the answer is B.`,
            image: ["/assets/national-I/2021_national-I_6_solution.png"]
        }
