        topic: "Descriptive/Laboratory",
        question: String.raw`A solution that may contain either 0.1~M \ce{Ag+(aq)}, 0.1~M \ce{Pb^2+(aq)}, or both, is treated with 1~M aqueous \ce{HCl}. A white precipitate forms which does not appear to dissolve in hot water. Which conclusion about the cations present may be drawn?`,
